as people in kind of overseas territories, and that therefore there is no kind of British citizenship in the way that there's American or French citizenship. And therefore, he comes to worry about what is it that distinguishes people who live in, say, England from people who live in the Caribbean, legally. Yeah, he's obsessed with all the sort of legal details of these kinds of things. So a really good example, actually. Slightly tangential to what you're talking about is he has a massive being his bonus about the queen's official title because it says that she's the queen of her other realms and territories. And he says, well, does this mean? It's meaningless. Her other realms and territories. It could mean anything. Remorseless logic, driving him mad.
就像海外领土的人一样，因此没有像美国或法国公民身份那样的英国公民身份。因此，他开始担心，在法律上，居住在例如英格兰的人与居住在加勒比海的人有什么区别。是的，他痴迷于这类事情的所有法律细节。所以一个很好的例子，实际上。与你谈论的内容略有偏离的是，他因为女王的官方头衔而有一个巨大的心结，因为它说她是她其他王国和领土的女王。他说，嗯，这意味着什么？这毫无意义。她其他王国和领土。它可能意味着任何事情。无情的逻辑，让他发疯。

