128
01:06:07.000 --> 01:06:53.000
editorial, that people had the impression that I hated black and Asian people, that they had a, they were right to be afraid of me, right? I would be really troubled by that. And I would be desperate to show people that I wasn't racist, you know, that I was a, I was a kindly person. I mean, even if I'm not a terribly kindly person, I'm definitely not a racist person. Anyway, I wouldn't want people to come to that conclusion, but Powell never seems to give their anxieties any thought. And I think that is a massive failure of empathy, personally. Anyway, what about his legacy? I think an obvious, unanticipated consequence of this speech in the furorre is that his exile, as it were, is so complete that it deters other politicians
社论的话，人们认为我讨厌黑人和亚裔，他们有理由害怕我，对吧？我会为此感到非常不安。我会拼命向人们证明我不是种族主义者，你知道，我是一个善良的人。我的意思是，即使我不是一个非常善良的人，我也绝对不是一个种族主义者。总之，我不想让人们得出那个结论，但鲍威尔似乎从未考虑过他们的焦虑。我个人认为，这是同理心的巨大缺失。总之，他的遗产是什么？我认为这次演讲和骚乱的一个明显的、未预料到的后果是，他的流放是如此彻底，以至于它阻止了其他政治家

129
01:06:53.000 --> 01:07:29.000
from even mentioning immigration. So I think in the 70s and 80s, the potential for kind of populist anti-immigration politics was always there, but it's really remarkable how nobody exploits it. Margaret Thatcher, who in many ways is a kind of pal disciple, does it just once. In 1978, in the Ilford by-election, she gave an interview and she said, People are really rather afraid that this country might be rather swamped by people with a different culture. There's a massive furority, backlash among her senior colleagues. She never does it again.
甚至提到移民。所以我认为在70年代和80年代，民粹主义反移民政治的潜力一直存在，但没有人利用它，这真的很了不起。玛格丽特·撒切尔在很多方面是鲍威尔的信徒，她只做了一次。1978年，在伊尔福德补选中，她接受采访时说，人们确实非常担心这个国家可能会被不同文化的人淹没。她的高级同事们反应强烈，引发了巨大的骚乱。她再也没有这样做过。

130
01:07:29.000 --> 01:08:13.000
